TWIN OPERATIVES: VAULT NINE
A small, single-file game written entirely in Paracine.

Two operatives, Rhea and Vex, are trapped inside a secured vault. An automated turret attacks them while they attempt to escape.

You control their actions through command-line moves. Win by either destroying the turret or hacking three security locks.




Download Twin Operatives (.pcn)




How to play
blast

Rhea

Deals 3 turret damage.


hack

Vex

Unlocks 1 of 3 security locks.


guard

Rhea

Deals 1 damage and blocks retaliation.


patch

Vex

Restores 4 health; one use.



Compile the file with your Paracine compiler:







BASH:
paracine build twin_operatives.pcn



Then play by specifying actions in their execution order:



BASH:
twin_operatives.exe blast hack guard hack hack



This sequence successfully breaches all three locks. Each run processes the supplied moves in order, so changing the sequence changes the outcome.

Language features demonstrated: modules, imports, typed variables, mutable state, Boolean conditions, structured iteration, text comparisons, effects, integer arithmetic, and explicit return values.

The source uses Paracine syntax and no C++, Python, external game engine, or custom modules.







Navigate in powershell to the pathe the game is stored. Type this in:

blast hack guard hack hack



You should see:

TWIN OPERATIVES: VAULT NINE
