5. Vex hacks the third lock. Victory!

The standout detail is that the turret correctly stopped attacking after the final hack. Your nested conditions, mutable state, and victory logic worked together exactly as intended.
One more engineering test
Now test the alternative victory path:



POWERSHELL:
& "D:\twin_operatives.exe" blast blast blast



This checks whether eliminating the turret correctly terminates combat without unnecessary retaliation.

You now have concrete runtime evidence of a working Paracine game, not merely a compiler success message.

Next milestone: Turn Twin Operatives into an actual interactive, turn-based game, where you enter moves during execution, choose between Rhea and Vex, fight different enemies, navigate rooms and complete missions—all written strictly in Paracine.







